  "question": "**Case Study 2: Over Speed Violation Detection System**<br /><br />A camera is installed on a pole at the height of 5 m. A car moves away from the pole with speed 20 m/s and angle of elevation of the camera from the car is $\\theta$.<br /><br />(i) Express $\\theta$ in terms of x.<br /><br />(ii) Find $\\frac{d\\theta}{dx}$.<br /><br />(iii) (a) Find $\\frac{d\\theta}{dt}$.<br /><br />OR<br /><br />(iii) (b) If $\\frac{d\\theta}{dt}=-\\frac{3}{101}$ rad/s at x=50 m, find the speed of the car.",
  "answeroption": "D",
  "explanation": "(i) $\\theta=\\tan^{-1}(\\frac{5}{x})$<br /><br />(ii) $\\frac{d\\theta}{dx}=-\\frac{5}{x^2+25}$<br /><br />(iii)(a) $\\frac{d\\theta}{dt}=-\\frac{100}{x^2+25}$<br /><br />OR<br /><br />(iii)(b) speed $=15$ m/s.",
